":{"login":"Bip901","id":74911767,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0OTExNzY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74911767?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bip901","html_url":"https://github.com/Bip901","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bip901/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bip901/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bip901/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bip901/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bip901/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bip901/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bip901/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bip901/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bip901/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-21T15:19:17Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T15:21:11Z","body":"> How do other projects bridge this issue? Rewrite using a new library, or don't use browsers for games with networking?\n\nThis is a solved problem, the dotnet runtime is supposed to seamlessly use the WebAsswmbly implementation of System.Net.Http, which injects `fetch` calls. It's just that Godot fails linking to the WebAssembly HTTP implementation properly.\n\nOther .NET-on-the-web projects like Avalonia/Blazor work fine using the same codebase for both PC and Browser.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3427224454/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]